WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:11.140
FedRAMP Moderate is a commonly used baseline for cloud services supporting federal use cases with meaningful security, privacy, operational, or mission impact.

2
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:21.080
It connects impact categorization to security control expectations, engineering implementation, assessment evidence, authorization support, and continuous monitoring.

3
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:26.540
Moderate is common because many federal services fall into that risk space, not because the work is simple.

4
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:34.100
The most important concepts are scope, impact, implementation, evidence, and operations.

5
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.720
Scope defines the cloud service offering and its boundary.

6
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.260
Impact explains why Moderate is the right risk category.

7
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.120
Implementation shows how controls work in the real system.

8
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.860
Evidence supports assessment conclusions.

9
00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:54.040
Operations keep the control environment healthy after authorization support activities are complete.

10
00:00:54.320 --> 00:01:00.160
Success depends on shared responsibility and accurate documentation.

11
00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:07.140
Providers, platforms, customers, assessors, and authorizing officials all have different roles.

12
00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.880
Inherited controls must be traceable.

13
00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.140
Customer responsibilities must be clear.

14
00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.960
Documentation must match the live architecture and operating processes.

15
00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:23.380
A Moderate story is only credible when the words, diagrams, evidence, and system behavior align.

16
00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:26.060
The goal is not simply to pass a review.

17
00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.800
The goal is to help federal stakeholders make informed risk decisions about a cloud service.

18
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:43.460
A strong Moderate program gives those stakeholders a clear view of the service boundary, control implementation, assessment evidence, known risks, remediation work, and ongoing monitoring.

19
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.920
That is the practical value of understanding FedRAMP Moderate.
